/* ---------------------------------------------------- the press assets
 * What goes in the picture holes of the reel, carried as data rather than
 * as files.
 *
 * NOT because a file would be slower — because a file cannot be used at
 * all here. The galley is a canvas that is uploaded to WebGL as a
 * texture, and the catalogue reads the same canvas back with toDataURL.
 * Both of those throw on a TAINTED canvas, and an image loaded from disk
 * taints one: under file:// every document is its own opaque origin, so
 * the bench pages — which are opened straight off the disk, not served —
 * lose the whole reel the moment a real photograph is drawn into it. A
 * data URI has no origin to be foreign to, so it taints nothing, and the
 * same file then works served, unserved, and on Pages.
 *
 * Nothing here was drawn by hand. Sources are named on each entry, and
 * they are captures: bench material standing in for work Splash has not
 * made yet. The Information is Beautiful graphics are CC BY-NC.
 *
 * GENERATED. Re-make it from landing/press/ rather than editing it.
 */
